NAME: a Silk-style paper in RED
DESCRIPTION: eight processes copy the paper through the A-field postincrement (}) of its SPL cell, which RED writes on numbers and labels since d-7d2612-0e831c; phase-2 archetype suite (i-7d2612-34b61d), see behtests/archetype_silk.beh
SRC:
(seq
  (SPL (Dir 1))
  (SPL (Dir 1))
  (SPL (Dir 1))
  (label silk)
  (SPL (Ind 0) (} 2731))
  (MOV I (} silk) (Inc silk))
  (MOV I bomb (Inc 2000))
  (label bomb)
  (DAT 0 0))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

  SPL    $1     , #0     
  SPL    $1     , #0     
  SPL    $1     , #0     
silk  
  SPL    @0     , }2731  
  MOV.I  }silk  , >silk  
  MOV.I  $bomb  , >2000  
bomb  
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     